# Begin with the End in Mind: Final Project Overview

Unit 5: Designing Reliable Apps with AI and APIs culminates with a final **Explore-Style Web App** project.

## Tap for More: Explore-Style App

In the *Tap for More* project, students design an interactive explore-style app that fetches live data from an external API and presents it in a grid of cards with a detail view. Inspired by apps like Pinterest, Yelp, TikTok, and news feeds, students curate content and design how users explore and learn more about individual items.

---

## Sample project

<iframe src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit5AIF2/museum-explorer-app.html" width="100%" height="900" style="border:none;"></iframe>

---

**When Project Begins:** Final three lessons of the unit

The project extends over multiple class periods following introductory lessons on `async/await`, error handling, and working with JSON data from APIs.



## What success looks like

>  **By the end, students will:**
> - Fetch and display live data from an external API
> - Build an explore-style interface with a “Tap for More” detail view
> - Communicate system status using loading indicators, empty states, and error messages
> - Design defensively to keep apps usable when data is delayed, incomplete, or unavailable
> - Reflect on the reliability, ownership, and risks of relying on external data sources

---

This project gives students an authentic opportunity to combine technical skills and design thinking while building apps that depend on real-world data and AI-powered systems.

## Now, let’s see how we get here!


